WEBVTT

00:02:10.208 --> 00:02:11.676
<i>They're finally off to battle.</i>

00:02:11.743 --> 00:02:15.543
Even the fire dragon can't
stand up to an army this big!

00:02:15.613 --> 00:02:18.082
Long live King Kashue!

00:02:33.231 --> 00:02:36.064
What?!
Priest Hobb has joined Ashram?!

00:02:44.075 --> 00:02:48.137
Kashue and Parn, having gone to the
shrine of Myrii, the god of war...

00:02:48.213 --> 00:02:50.978
...to ask Priest Hobb
for his assistance...

00:02:51.049 --> 00:02:54.917
...have discovered that Hobb
has gone of f with Ashram.

00:02:55.653 --> 00:03:00.215
I never expected him to help Ashram...
A foolish oversight on my part.

00:03:04.095 --> 00:03:06.189
King Kashue...

00:03:10.401 --> 00:03:13.496
Don't let it bother you, Parn.

00:03:14.772 --> 00:03:18.470
It just means the number of enemies
we must defeat has grown by one.

00:03:18.543 --> 00:03:22.537
Although, to be honest, I'd prefer
not to make an enemy of him...

00:03:22.614 --> 00:03:26.983
In any case, defeating the fire
dragon Shooting Star comes first!

00:03:27.585 --> 00:03:29.451
Yes, sir!

00:03:31.856 --> 00:03:33.654
Parn...

00:03:34.225 --> 00:03:35.420
Shirts?!

00:03:35.493 --> 00:03:38.895
It's too bad, Parn.
Now we have to split up.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:39.929
Y- Yeah, I guess.

00:03:39.998 --> 00:03:43.127
Shirts, it's time for your
group to leave, too, isn't it?

00:03:43.201 --> 00:03:44.498
Should you really be
wasting time like this?

00:03:44.569 --> 00:03:47.595
| get you, Miss Crabby EIf.
See you!

00:03:52.677 --> 00:03:56.204
What's wrong, Deed?
You look sort of irritated.

00:03:56.514 --> 00:03:58.676
Huh? Uh-uh, it's nothing.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.983
Elves are forest sprites, so the
desert climate doesn't really suit us.

00:04:03.054 --> 00:04:04.783
| see...

00:04:04.856 --> 00:04:08.850
I'm sorry for all those times I took
you out into the desert, Deed.

00:04:08.926 --> 00:04:11.759
Oh, no. Don't worry about it.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.044
There they go.

00:04:27.111 --> 00:04:30.308
While Parn and the others
are off slaying Shooting Star...

00:04:30.381 --> 00:04:32.873
...we have our own job to do.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.941
Yes... That's right.

00:04:35.019 --> 00:04:37.181
Well, then, we should be off, too.

00:04:37.255 --> 00:04:40.122
Okay, Leader. Give us your orders.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.698
Let's move out.
To the free city of Raiden.

00:05:02.413 --> 00:05:04.575
It... It's them! The pirates!

00:05:04.649 --> 00:05:06.174
Help us!!

00:05:11.122 --> 00:05:13.113
What a haul! What a haul!

00:05:13.925 --> 00:05:16.622
Those guys were such pushovers
it was almost boring!

00:05:17.428 --> 00:05:20.329
Come on!
Get this booty unloaded!

00:05:24.035 --> 00:05:27.938
Looks like that help we got
from the Marmo was worth it.

00:05:28.005 --> 00:05:32.567
No kidding. At first I thought this
wasn't gonna be a profitable job.

00:05:32.977 --> 00:05:36.436
All we do is wait for Sir Ashram.
However...

00:05:36.514 --> 00:05:38.778
...this is turning out
to be a pretty sweet job!

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:39.976
Yeah.

00:05:40.051 --> 00:05:42.247
Boss! It's Sir Ashram...

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.914
Sir Ashram's arrived here!

00:05:44.989 --> 00:05:47.117
8- Sir Ashram?!

00:05:54.098 --> 00:05:57.068
W- We've been waiting
for you, Sir Ashram!

00:05:57.135 --> 00:05:59.832
I'm glad to see you're okay.

00:06:03.207 --> 00:06:05.539
Glad to see me, eh?

00:06:09.347 --> 00:06:13.215
I never told you people to start
playing pirate around here!

00:06:13.284 --> 00:06:15.446
B- But, when we're not fighting,

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.852
we have to steal
to support the ship!

00:06:18.256 --> 00:06:22.215
Naturally, we'll split half our haul
with you Marmo gentlemen.

00:06:22.293 --> 00:06:26.787
Enough! Just get the ship ready!
Those are your orders now, Alhaib!

00:06:28.599 --> 00:06:29.862
Y- You mean...?

00:06:29.934 --> 00:06:32.960
Once we're ready, we're going
to Blue Dragon Island.

00:06:33.037 --> 00:06:35.267
To meet the sea dragon Abram.

00:06:35.339 --> 00:06:36.101
Now hurry!

00:06:36.174 --> 00:06:37.073
Y- Yes, sir! At once!

00:06:37.141 --> 00:06:38.575
At once!

00:06:41.712 --> 00:06:45.512
We have but one objective:
The Scepter of Domination!

00:06:46.517 --> 00:06:50.112
If Abram doesn't have it,
we'll pull out at once!

00:06:50.188 --> 00:06:52.350
And if he DOES have it?

00:06:52.423 --> 00:06:59.329
Then we must fight him.
80 long as he is under the spell...

00:06:59.397 --> 00:07:03.095
...of the ancient kingdom, his only
purpose is to guard that treasure.

00:07:05.102 --> 00:07:10.006
Win once, win all.
It's a proper way to look at things.

00:07:11.909 --> 00:07:15.402
It's not as though a dragon
can't be reasoned with.

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:19.212
First, though, we must determine
if he has the treasure.

00:07:19.283 --> 00:07:23.277
It looks as though I'll have to
leave that up to you, Groder.

00:07:23.354 --> 00:07:26.051
Leave it to me, Sir Ashram.

00:07:27.124 --> 00:07:29.115
Where are you going?

00:07:29.193 --> 00:07:32.060
Well, even a minor sorcerer
like me has other interests.

00:07:32.129 --> 00:07:35.724
The unusual land formations
around here intrigue me...

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.132
...so I was hoping to take a walk
and get a closer look at them.

00:07:38.202 --> 00:07:42.196
I see. Just be careful you
don't fall of f of the cliffs.

00:07:42.573 --> 00:07:46.441
And be sure also to give my
regards to Master Wagnard.

00:08:00.925 --> 00:08:04.759
Sir Ashram is preparing to meet
Abram on Blue Dragon Island.

00:08:04.829 --> 00:08:08.732
He will surely deliver to you
that which you desire, Master.

00:08:09.433 --> 00:08:11.834
However, don't make light of him.

00:08:11.903 --> 00:08:15.999
Sir Ashram seems to have
realized what your plans are.

00:08:16.541 --> 00:08:20.136
If he couldn't do that,
he'd be of no use to me.

00:08:20.811 --> 00:08:24.543
Don't forget we need
the Soul Crystal Ball as well.

00:08:24.682 --> 00:08:28.277
| pray your next report
will be a favorable one.

00:08:28.386 --> 00:08:29.854
By your command.

00:08:34.292 --> 00:08:37.887
Oh, Kardis! The time of
your resurrection is near!

00:08:37.962 --> 00:08:41.296
When that happens, I shall gain
an understanding of all spells!

00:08:41.365 --> 00:08:43.959
I shall become the supreme being!

00:08:54.512 --> 00:08:57.846
That man Groder can not be trusted.

00:08:58.849 --> 00:09:02.615
He's hiding secrets somewhere
deep inside his heart.

00:09:02.987 --> 00:09:04.921
I know that.

00:09:04.989 --> 00:09:09.187
It's not just him. I'm suspicious
of Gaberra and Astar as well.

00:09:10.261 --> 00:09:13.094
Aside from the mercenaries
Smeddy and Gilram...

00:09:13.164 --> 00:09:15.690
...the others were sent
by ones like me,

00:09:15.766 --> 00:09:18.133
rulers of Marmo,
and I don't trust them.

00:09:18.836 --> 00:09:21.100
In that case,
you should be very careful.

00:09:21.172 --> 00:09:25.439
A man who fears petty betrayal
isn't worthy of the Marmo crown.

00:09:25.843 --> 00:09:28.312
That's part of what it is
to be a king.

00:09:28.379 --> 00:09:30.074
As you say.

00:09:30.147 --> 00:09:33.981
It is in the nature of a hero
to ignore trivial matters.

00:09:34.051 --> 00:09:35.450
Quite right...

00:09:35.519 --> 00:09:39.149
And a true hero always gets
what he sets out to gain!

00:09:53.904 --> 00:09:57.568
Orson and the others have arrived
at the free city of Raiden but...

00:09:57.642 --> 00:10:01.306
...with the panic among the sailors
caused by the recent pirate raids...

00:10:01.379 --> 00:10:05.111
...they cannot secure a
ship to Blue Dragon Island.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.820
Damn! It's not working.

00:10:18.963 --> 00:10:22.922
Dammit! How can sailors be
so scared of some pirates?!

00:10:25.036 --> 00:10:27.198
You can't really blame them for it.

00:10:27.271 --> 00:10:30.502
Not everyone can be as strong
as you are.

00:10:30.574 --> 00:10:34.738
In that case, we should take care
of these pirates ourselves!

00:10:37.081 --> 00:10:38.515
Take care of them...?

00:10:38.582 --> 00:10:43.349
How can you say that?
Have you forgotten our mission?

00:10:43.421 --> 00:10:47.483
Yeah! Really, this is why I hate war
happy mercenaries like you!

00:10:47.558 --> 00:10:48.548
What did you call us?!

00:10:48.626 --> 00:10:52.290
In that case,
why don't I help you out? Hm?

00:10:52.897 --> 00:10:54.092
Who are you?

00:10:54.165 --> 00:10:57.658
You're a meadow sprite.
A grass runner, right?

00:10:57.902 --> 00:11:00.200
They call me Maar the Bard.

00:11:00.271 --> 00:11:04.208
Oh, but I'm not just a poet.
I know all sorts of things!

00:11:04.642 --> 00:11:07.907
For instance,
how to find the pirates...

00:11:08.446 --> 00:11:09.379
Really?!

00:11:09.447 --> 00:11:13.350
Of course! And in return,
you take me with you! Okay?

00:11:13.484 --> 00:11:15.077
Whoa!

00:11:15.152 --> 00:11:18.952
Be serious! You think we'd believe
a cock and bull story like that?!

00:11:19.023 --> 00:11:21.185
What're you doing?!
Lemme go!

00:11:21.258 --> 00:11:22.692
Cecil, really...

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:28.062
Ooh... If Parn was here, he'd be
all for taking out those pirates.

00:11:28.332 --> 00:11:30.630
Yes, you're right.

00:11:32.336 --> 00:11:35.931
Then let's take care
of those pirates ourselves.

00:11:45.082 --> 00:11:48.814
Wh- What are you saying?!
Are you sure about this?!

00:11:49.286 --> 00:11:50.720
It's really simple.

00:11:50.788 --> 00:11:54.224
As long as the pirates are active,
we won't be able to get a ship.

00:11:54.291 --> 00:11:57.090
Therefore, our only choice
is to get rid of the pirates.

00:11:57.161 --> 00:11:59.823
W- Well, I guess
you're right, but...

00:11:59.897 --> 00:12:02.332
Your information about
the pirates is correct, right?

00:12:02.399 --> 00:12:05.994
There aren't many of us, but if we
catch the enemy, unaware, we could win.

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:08.164
This guy knows
what he's talking about.

00:12:08.239 --> 00:12:09.468
One more thing.

00:12:10.474 --> 00:12:11.498
One more thing?

00:12:12.076 --> 00:12:14.408
If we capture the pirates' ship...

00:12:14.478 --> 00:12:17.971
...we save ourselves the trouble of
outfitting a ship of our own.

00:12:18.048 --> 00:12:20.176
That's right...

00:12:21.385 --> 00:12:22.716
Okay, it's settled, then!

00:12:22.787 --> 00:12:25.586
Nobody's got a beef with
our leader's plan, do they?

00:12:25.656 --> 00:12:28.785
It looks like I really was right
in choosing you to lead.

00:12:28.859 --> 00:12:30.850
You really are just like Parn.

00:12:30.928 --> 00:12:33.863
Now that that's settled,
let's have a pre-battle celebration!

00:12:33.931 --> 00:12:36.298
Tonight, we drink and make merry!

00:12:36.367 --> 00:12:39.098
In that case, you can use this!

00:12:40.371 --> 00:12:43.636
Hey! That's my wallet!
When did you...?!

00:12:44.542 --> 00:12:45.270
Whoops! Uh-oh!

00:12:45.342 --> 00:12:48.107
Why, you...! Come back here!

00:12:48.412 --> 00:12:49.675
Orson...

00:12:49.747 --> 00:12:52.614
Did that talk before
make you nervous?

00:12:52.683 --> 00:12:54.082
That talk before?

00:12:54.151 --> 00:12:56.643
When I said that Parn
would want to fight the pirates.

00:12:56.720 --> 00:13:00.714
Did you go along with my idea because
you wanted to show Parn up a little?

00:13:00.791 --> 00:13:03.522
No, it's just as I explained it.

00:13:03.594 --> 00:13:04.254
No other reason?

00:13:04.461 --> 00:13:05.929
No other reason.

00:13:05.996 --> 00:13:09.364
Sheesh! You should be
a LITTLE jealous, you know!

00:13:09.433 --> 00:13:13.370
You make a girl feel like
she's not worth fighting over!

00:13:16.106 --> 00:13:19.599
| wonder how Slayn and
the others are doing now.

00:13:19.677 --> 00:13:21.805
Do you think Orson's doing
a good job?

00:13:22.746 --> 00:13:27.240
They're fine. I'm sure Slayn
chose the right leader for them.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:33.186
And if we can free Orson from the
control of the spirit of anger...

00:13:33.257 --> 00:13:36.022
...then I think Leylia will finally
be healed of the guilt over...

00:13:36.093 --> 00:13:39.028
...what happened while her mind was
under Karla's control.

00:13:39.096 --> 00:13:41.087
That's what Slayn hopes, anyway.

00:13:41.165 --> 00:13:43.634
Yes, that's one of
Slayn's good qualities.

00:13:43.701 --> 00:13:46.636
He goes so far out of his way
to help others...

00:13:46.704 --> 00:13:49.696
Humans really are a strange breed.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:53.804
Almost incomprehensible
to an elf like me.

00:13:55.846 --> 00:13:59.248
His good quality...
Yeah, I agree with you.

00:13:59.316 --> 00:14:02.581
He'd prefer to just grow enough
much food as he needed and...

00:14:02.653 --> 00:14:03.984
...teach children to read.

00:14:04.054 --> 00:14:07.922
That's really the life Slayn
would choose for himself.

00:14:08.993 --> 00:14:10.483
But still...

00:14:10.561 --> 00:14:13.553
The times won't allow that.

00:14:14.932 --> 00:14:16.661
Besides that...

00:14:17.501 --> 00:14:20.527
How would you like to become a king?

00:14:20.604 --> 00:14:24.063
While there are still things
| can change on my own...

00:14:24.141 --> 00:14:27.543
...should concentrate on them.
Right Deed?

00:14:34.585 --> 00:14:35.450
What's wrong?

00:14:35.519 --> 00:14:37.749
Parn... Look there.

00:14:37.821 --> 00:14:39.789
What's...?!

00:14:52.102 --> 00:14:55.732
This is Shooting Star's doing...
It's a massacre!

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:03.069
The dragon's hunting ground...
A fitting name for this place!

00:15:03.147 --> 00:15:05.878
We'll launch our attack here!
Is that understood?!

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:08.078
You really think he'll return?

00:15:08.152 --> 00:15:09.813
He will. Without a doubt.

00:15:09.887 --> 00:15:12.413
It seems the one thing
he can't stand is...

00:15:12.489 --> 00:15:15.049
...humans intruding
into his feeding grounds.

00:15:42.886 --> 00:15:45.082
Mmm... Orson...

00:15:47.191 --> 00:15:50.320
C'mon... You call yourself a man...?

00:16:00.437 --> 00:16:02.633
You'll catch a cold.

00:16:02.706 --> 00:16:04.572
Mmm... Warm...

00:16:13.117 --> 00:16:15.984
You should be a LITTLE
jealous, you know!

00:16:16.053 --> 00:16:17.214
Don't worry, though.

00:16:17.287 --> 00:16:20.154
I'm sure this journey will get
your old feelings back.

00:16:20.224 --> 00:16:23.717
I believe in the strength
of your will.

00:16:26.563 --> 00:16:28.463
Should I try facing it?

00:16:28.532 --> 00:16:31.092
The true face of rage...

00:16:37.207 --> 00:16:38.902
My sister...

00:16:38.976 --> 00:16:43.607
It started here. All memories
after it are controlled by rage...

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.235
Orson... Forgive me.

00:17:05.869 --> 00:17:07.530
Rage...

00:17:07.604 --> 00:17:08.935
Rage...

00:17:09.006 --> 00:17:11.998
St- Stop it... Stop it! Stop it!

00:17:15.846 --> 00:17:18.611
Stop it! Stop it!

00:17:24.888 --> 00:17:26.913
Rage...

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:29.755
Destroy...everything...

00:17:33.797 --> 00:17:36.892
Rage... Destroy everything...

00:17:37.634 --> 00:17:40.228
Rage... Destroy...

00:17:40.771 --> 00:17:43.001
Orson... Forgive me.

00:17:43.073 --> 00:17:45.007
NO!

00:18:05.696 --> 00:18:07.721
That was too close...

00:18:07.798 --> 00:18:11.564
| can't try a dangerous
test like that again.

00:18:12.136 --> 00:18:14.798
But I'm sure I heard it.

00:18:14.872 --> 00:18:18.604
That was the voice
of the spirit of anger...

00:18:31.889 --> 00:18:33.755
Let's go.

00:18:52.276 --> 00:18:54.643
Here he comes!

00:19:02.152 --> 00:19:03.517
That's him...

00:19:03.587 --> 00:19:05.783
Shooting Star...

00:19:16.767 --> 00:19:18.701
At last...

00:19:18.802 --> 00:19:21.203
That's who we're facing.

00:19:21.271 --> 00:19:23.433
But... It's so big!

00:19:42.759 --> 00:19:43.726
Welcome...

00:19:43.794 --> 00:19:45.489
...to Lodoss Island!

00:19:45.562 --> 00:19:46.927
And now, what
you've been waiting for...

00:19:46.997 --> 00:19:48.658
The second part of the show!

00:19:58.408 --> 00:20:01.378
Hi there! Sorry to keep you waiting!
Welcome to the first annual...

00:20:01.445 --> 00:20:07.179
...Make Solemn Orson Who's Forgotten
His Feelings Laugh Contest!

00:20:17.094 --> 00:20:18.061
Okay, then...

00:20:18.128 --> 00:20:21.154
Okay, let's have a hand
for entry number one!

00:20:21.231 --> 00:20:23.165
Go for it!

00:20:35.545 --> 00:20:38.412
If you keep swinging
that sword (800DO) around...

00:20:38.482 --> 00:20:40.951
...you're gonna cause
some trouble (SOODOOSHII)!

00:20:41.018 --> 00:20:42.850
Okay, next contestant!

00:20:42.919 --> 00:20:45.616
I am the spirit of wind.
Hey, Orson!

00:20:45.689 --> 00:20:47.817
| can teach you (SEIRETE)
all about spirits (SEIREI)!

00:20:48.659 --> 00:20:50.058
Next, please...

00:20:51.561 --> 00:20:53.757
Okay, let's get the show
on the road.

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:57.266
"Hey, lady! A magician(MAHOU TSUKALI)
has moved into the lot next door!"

00:20:57.334 --> 00:21:00.031
"Oh, my! Let's leave him alone!"
(MAA, HOU-TTE OKIMASHOU)

00:21:00.103 --> 00:21:02.504
That's the joke, folks.

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:08.840
Can't ANYBODY make you laugh?

00:21:08.912 --> 00:21:10.971
You're all amateurs,
everybody!

00:21:11.048 --> 00:21:13.278
Let ME have a crack at him!

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.749
King Kashue!

00:21:14.818 --> 00:21:17.583
Orson (ORUSAN), Mama's going out!

00:21:17.654 --> 00:21:21.056
Can you watch the
house (ORUSUBAN) for me?!

00:21:28.165 --> 00:21:31.260
Agh! Gimme a
chance to try it again!

00:21:32.135 --> 00:21:34.570
Orson... ORUSUBAN...

00:22:59.956 --> 00:23:03.620
At last, the time to battle
Shooting Star has come!

00:23:03.693 --> 00:23:05.593
Flying in the air on huge wings!

00:23:05.662 --> 00:23:07.562
Incinerating the ground
with his fire breath!

00:23:07.631 --> 00:23:10.225
The soldiers of Flaim
fall in huge numbers!

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:14.601
At the same time, Orson faces the
ghostly light of the Demon Sword!

00:23:15.338 --> 00:23:18.273
Next time, on Record of Lodoss War-
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight:

00:23:18.341 --> 00:23:21.140
Demon Sword...
The Power to Crush Souls
